# Lexer token-type ID golden policy (Phase 2.6+)

When adding lexer tokens (e.g. `LEFT_BRACKET` / `RIGHT_BRACKET` for array subscript), ANTLR renumbers token type IDs. Golden tests embed those IDs in position strings like `<433>`.

## Do

- Update goldens **only** for tests added or changed to prove the current grammar extension (e.g. new `SqlEventWalkerArraySubscriptTests`).
- At the **end** of the lexer/grammar work (when the user says we're done), take one pass to update token string rule IDs across the suite — **after** talking to the user first.

## Do not

- Bulk-update token IDs across the full test suite mid-task.
- Re-run the entire walker golden corpus expecting to auto-fix `<nnn>` token references.

## Automatic required process for every lexer addition

Trigger this process whenever a task adds lexer items, even if the user does not
ask for a token-ID report. Capture the before image **before changing the
grammar**, then regenerate and capture the after image. Do not overwrite the
before image with regenerated output. If changes already exist, identify the
pre-addition revision and generate its lexer in an isolated worktree; never
guess the old constants or disturb the current checkout.

1. Add new lexer keywords at the end of the late-keyword block, immediately before
   `Identifier`. Preserve existing lexer order.
2. Use the count of inserted lexer terms as the expected shift increment.
3. Build a complete old/new lexer-ID worklist from generated ANTLR lexer class
   constants (not from failing test output).
4. Include the entire sorted worklist (highest new token ID to lowest) in the
   **final response/summary**, with token **name + before ID + after ID + delta**,
   the added token names, and the expected increment. Include all existing tokens
   following the additions, starting with `Identifier`, through the final token,
   including comments, whitespace, and skip tokens absent from failing tests.
   Never truncate the worklist or replace it with a link or selected examples.
5. Verify the observed shifts match the expected increment and earlier token IDs
   are unchanged. If not, report the discrepancy explicitly; do not infer a
   uniform replacement. If no IDs shift, explicitly report that result.
6. This is the developer's manual IDE worklist. Do not automatically modify
   existing golden token IDs.

### Commands

```bash
# 1) Capture old generated lexer constants before edits
mvn -pl parse -DskipTests generate-sources
cp parse/target/generated-sources/antlr4/sql/SQLSelectParserLexer.java /tmp/sql-lexer.before.java

# 2) Make lexer keyword additions, then capture new generated lexer constants
mvn -pl parse -DskipTests generate-sources
cp parse/target/generated-sources/antlr4/sql/SQLSelectParserLexer.java /tmp/sql-lexer.after.java

# 3) Produce comprehensive manual worklist
python3 tools/token_id_worklist_from_vocab.py \
  /tmp/sql-lexer.before.java \
  /tmp/sql-lexer.after.java
```

Do not derive the replacement set from runTests-only mismatches; that can hide
unseen token-ID shifts and lead to incorrect blanket replacements.
